{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"mola","tool":"write_file","arguments":{"machine_id":"020eec67-d833-46ea-93e0-b49bc3989f97","path":"~/benchmark/social-report.md","content":"## Major themes\n\n- Acme Robotics’ discussion centers on the Rover Mini launch, with interest in its compact design and quiet motors. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/launch.html\n- Customer conversation emphasizes ease of onboarding and documentation, alongside operational support and connectivity problems. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n- Market discussion positions Acme’s SDK documentation against BetaBot Pocket’s longer battery life. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/market.html\n\n## Notable discussions\n\n- The Rover Mini launch announcement received replies asking whether Linux SDK support will ship. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/launch.html\n- Customers specifically discuss fast setup, clear Python examples, delayed replacement parts, and Wi-Fi reconnect failures after sleep. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n- Customers compare Rover Mini with BetaBot Pocket, citing Acme’s SDK documentation and BetaBot’s longer battery life. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/market.html\n\n## Recurring praise\n\n- Replies praise the Rover Mini’s compact design and quiet motors. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/launch.html\n- Customers praise fast setup and clear Python examples. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n- Acme is praised for SDK documentation in comparisons with BetaBot Pocket. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/market.html\n\n## Recurring complaints\n\n- Customers report delayed replacement parts. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n- Customers report Wi-Fi reconnect failures after the device wakes from sleep. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n\n## Visible engagement\n\n- The Rover Mini launch shows 1,240 likes, 188 reposts, and 94 replies. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/launch.html\n- The customer discussion shows 310 likes and 86 replies. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n- The market discussion shows 73 likes and 22 reposts. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/market.html\n\n## Competitive mentions\n\n- BetaBot Pocket is the named competitor; the comparison highlights Acme’s SDK documentation and BetaBot’s longer battery life. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/market.html\n\n## Actionable observations\n\n1. Publish or clarify the Linux SDK support plan for Rover Mini, because multiple launch replies ask whether Linux support will ship. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/launch.html\n2. Investigate and address Wi-Fi reconnection after sleep, which customers identify as a recurring failure. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n3. Improve replacement-parts fulfillment or communicate clearer timelines, because delayed replacement parts are a recurring complaint. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n4. Preserve and extend the fast-setup experience and clear Python examples, which are recurring sources of customer praise. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/support.html\n5. Strengthen Rover Mini’s battery-life positioning or roadmap against BetaBot Pocket, which is mentioned as having longer battery life while Acme is praised for SDK documentation. Source: http://127.0.0.1:8765/market.html\n"},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
